large [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 3 red [[Cookbook:Bell Pepper|bell peppers]], chopped\n* 6 fresh [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]], chopped\n* Nigerian smoked [[Cookbook:Mackerel|Titus fish]], shredded\n* [[Cookbook:Ground Crayfish|Ground crayfish]] (optional)\n* Dried [[Cookbook:Shrimp|shrimp]] (optional)\n* Dried [[Cookbook:Chiles|chilli pepper]] (optional)\n* 6 [[Cookbook:Basil|Thai basil]] leaves, chopped\n==Equipment==\n*[[Cookbook:Blender|Blender]]\n*[[Cookbook:Cooktop|Cooktop]]\n*Knife\n*Turning spoon\n*[[Cookbook:Saucepan|Saucepan]]\n*Pot\n== Procedure ==\n#Wash the garden eggs with salt. Cut them into smaller pieces, and [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] in salted water for 10–15 minutes until soft.\n#Drain the garden egg, and [[Cookbook:Mashing|mash]] it.\n#Heat the palm oil in a pot over medium heat. Add the chopped onion, and cook until softened. Add the chopped pepper and tomatoes, and cook for 10 minutes.\n#Add the shredded fish, ground crayfish, dried shrimp, ground pepper, chopped basil, and salt to taste. Cover, and cook for 5 minutes.\n#Add the mashed garden egg. Cover, and cook for 5 minutes.\n#Serve with boiled plantain, yam, or potato.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using yam]]\n[[Category:Recipes using potato]]\n[[Category:Recipes using basil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using red bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground crayfish]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mackerel]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garden egg]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Garden Egg Stew","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"Garden eggs","sourceText":"Garden eggs","amountText":"Garden eggs","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"Salt","sourceText":"Salt","amountText":"Salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"¼ cup palm oil","sourceText":"¼ cup palm oil","amountText":"¼ cup palm oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null}